  "worked_solution": "First, let's re-write the expression, as follows:\n\n$$\ny=-\\sqrt{1-x}-1=-\\sqrt{-(x-1)}-1\n$$\n\nTo get the graph of $y=-\\sqrt{-(x-1)}-1,$ we can do the following transformations:\n\n- Take the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x}.$\n\n- Reflect the graph in the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=\\sqrt{-x}.$\n\nThe result is the solid blue curve shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14238243/assets/854a720d691342b87a7f390176cdc60cf5d68d8863a755fed8929dbd3fecd655.png)\n\n- Reflect the graph in the $x$-axis to get the graph of $y=-\\sqrt{-x}.$\n\nThe result is the solid blue curve shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14238243/assets/b5c145b598e3311edf3f9f6958245bd7a6b5a875e476d2f383e7c1c394f80538.png)\n\n- Translate the result to the right by $1$ unit to get the graph of $y=-\\sqrt{-(x-1)}.$\n\n- Translate the result down by $1$ unit to get the graph of $y=-\\sqrt{-(x-1)}-1.$\n\nThe result is the solid blue curve shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14238243/assets/7a7c548b2d93636bb00902b62a37fd75fc7aceea00c71574d7761b46775eb844.png)",
